  "body": "Follow-up to #2816 (ours), which left exactly six `d = 8` weight multisets of the weight-\u2264 7 basis open: `[7^5,6^5,1]`, `[7^6,6^4]`, `[7^8,5,4,1]`, `[7^8,5,5]`, `[7^8,6,3,1]`, `[7^8,6,4]`. All six are impossible. Adds only `research/one-sided-six-multisets/`; nothing existing changes.\n\n**Results** (setting, normalisation and `n_nf` as in #2816; P112, case (b), every `m`, char 0)\n- **Basis Lemma (PROVEN).** At `d = 8` the fundamental circuits of any \u03bb-basis give 8 *linearly independent* codeword directions `h_y` with `Off(h_y) \u2286 U_B \u222a \u039b(F_y)`.\n- **Lemma S66 / S66+t (CHECKED, two independent implementations).** For any two 6-dimensional label flats (plus one free line, chosen per direction, for S66+t) the qualifying directions span at most 3 dimensions (at most 6 directions). `s66.c` (C) and `indep.py` (Python, other coordinates and labels, direction list rebuilt from orthogonal root sums and checked against the theta counts) agree on all 159 orbit representatives of `V_1` against all 776,805 line sets of `V_2`; `indep.py` runs in 6 chunks and `check_logs.py` asserts exact coverage. Control: two 7-dimensional flats reach rank 8 (152 pairs).\n- **Theorem 6 (PROVEN from the above).** The six multisets cannot occur; 8 independent qualifying directions are needed and at most 3 exist.\n- **Consequences** (inherit #2816's reduction at cost 66; second, independent route via a `d = 0` Carrier Lemma for `\u03ba \u2264 2`, proved in the README): `\u0394 \u2264 2 \u21d2 n_nf \u2264 \u0394` (decoder level) and `\u03c1_0 \u2264 \u0394` (lift level).\n  - One-sided P112 decoders with `n_nf \u2264 3` non-full corrections (any number of full ones) cost **\u2265 64**; in general `\u2265 67 \u2212 n_nf` for `n_nf \u2265 3`, i.e. `\u2265 64 \u2212 max(0, n_nf \u2212 3) \u2265 59` (was `\u2265 64 \u2212 max(0, n_nf \u2212 2) \u2265 58`).\n  - Lift level: `cost_w(S) \u2265 64 + min(|I|, 3)` for every `S \u2287 \ud835\udc9e_{X_I}`; every lift of the E8 root code (E8/P120 decoder) costs **\u2265 67**, and **\u2265 72** unless the P112 restriction has `\u0394 \u2265 3`; gain-law form `|P120| \u2212 C(P120) \u2264 53`.\n\n**Caveats**\n- No \u03ba claim, no supplier word. One-sided (case (b)) decoders of P112 only; not two-sided, not case (c), not other units, characteristic 0.\n- `\u0394 \u2265 n_nf` for general `n_nf` stays OPEN; the root-swap family of #2816 is tight at `n_nf \u2264 4`. An extension to `\u0394 = 3` is in progress and is neither claimed nor used.\n- Inherited from #2816, cited and not recomputed: the DP/LP/Pencil/triple-rule survivor list (exactly these six at slack \u2264 2), the flat caps `g(1..8)`, `|Off| \u2265 53`, the circuit lemma.\n- `verify.sh` (fresh export, `nice -n 10`, at most 6 processes, each under `timeout 1200`, no wait loops): data regeneration, Parity-lemma search (rank-4 quadruples), `s66.c` (modes 0, t and the 7+7 control), `indep.py` in both modes, then one PASS/FAIL line per assertion. 1690 s wall (about 28 min under load), 14 PASS, 0 FAIL\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code; Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
